    description: "Titan’s plate-loaded chest press pairs two independent lever arms with an adjustable FID bench, so one machine covers flat, incline and decline pressing. Titan’s Amazon listing calls them converging lever arms; Titan’s own store says the independent arms follow a natural arc that mimics free weights, and does not use the word converging, so treat the path as something to try rather than a promise. Titan’s store and its Amazon listing agree on a 1,000 lb total capacity (the listing adds 500 lb per arm) and a 155 lb machine weight, and Titan’s store gives a footprint of 64 in wide by 63 to 77 in long, which Garage Gym Reviews repeats. The bench has 13 depth positions and the arms five positions, and Titan’s listing describes an 11-gauge steel frame, sealed bearings and safety stops. We saw it at $799.97 on Titan’s store, against $949.99, and $799.99 on Amazon on 9 November 2026. It replaces the Temple of Gainz Omnipress in this slot: the Omnipress is sold direct by Temple of Gainz, not on Amazon.",
  },
